# Byproducts of running the tools. External review 2026-08-03 hit these: a reviewer who rebuilds and
# re-runs the suite should end with a CLEAN tree, otherwise real changes hide among the noise and the
# release trail becomes hard to read.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# scratch files the build and test scripts write next to themselves
build/_*.mjs
build/_*.js
build/_*.html
build/_drift.*
build/_probe.mjs

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Dependencies are pinned by package-lock.json (exact versions + integrity hashes), which IS committed.
# The tree itself is not: it is large, platform-specific (a vendored esbuild binary is Windows-only, so
# it would not deliver cross-platform reproducibility anyway), and it churns on every `npm ci`, which
# makes real changes hard to see. The permanence promise does not depend on rebuilding this app: it rests
# on the words, the spec, and the standard-library-only Python recovery tool.
build/node_modules/

# NOTE, deliberately NOT ignored:
#   app/*.html          the released artifacts themselves; their hashes are published in the README
#   build/*.bundle.js   and build/claim-app.html, build/offline.html: the exact build outputs, kept so
#                       anyone can diff a rebuild against what we shipped without trusting our word
#   build/package-lock.json  the exact dependency tree, which is what makes builds reproducible
